message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "gasm-matched-extremes: supplementary code for the extremal elements of matched generalized alternating sign matrices"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-09"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "Kim"
    given-names: "Hwa Kyung"
    email: "indices@smu.ac.kr"
    affiliation: "Department of Mathematics Education, Sangmyung University, Seoul, Republic of Korea"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7727-9204"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23257733"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hwakyungkim/gasm-matched-extremes"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23257733"
abstract: >-
  JavaScript (Node.js) programs that enumerate matched classes of generalized
  alternating sign matrices, compute the arrays hi and lo, run the
  left-to-right sweep, and draw Hasse diagrams of the Bruhat order. They check
  the examples and the main statements of the paper "The extremal elements of
  the Bruhat lattice of generalized alternating sign matrices with matched
  boundary" on small cases.
keywords:
  - alternating sign matrix
  - generalized alternating sign matrix
  - Bruhat order
  - distributive lattice
  - six-vertex model
